cris: thread-local storage for CRIS v32 and v10

gcc has never generated TLS for CRIS, although binutils implements the
CRIS TLS ABI since 2008 and configure already has an assembler test for
it: variant II, the thread pointer in the upper 24 bits of $pid on v32.
v10 has no such register, so the thread pointer is r6 there, reserved
for it wherever TLS is enabled (the highest call-saved register without
a role: r0 is the PIC register, r7 the static chain, r8 the frame
pointer).  Older versions keep emulated TLS.  Generated are the models
of an executable: local-exec via sym:TPOFF and initial-exec via sym:IE,
or sym:TPOFFGOT with PIC, where gas does not take TPOFF.
general-dynamic, and with it dlopen of a library with TLS, is not done.

